  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\n1034mb surface ridge sits just to the northeast of the area.\nDewpoints are in the upper 30s to low 40s with clear skies and\ncalm winds. We appear on track for a very strong radiational\ncooling event through the next few hours which should lead to\nthe first widespread frost of the season.\n\nAnother strong upper ridge builds in over the central Plains\nthrough the next few days and keeps our pattern blocked up\nthrough the end of the week. We still look on track for dry and\npleasant conditions with seasonable highs in the 70s and lows in\nthe 40s. Guidance consensus is strong in keeping that pattern in\nplace at least into next weekend.",
